n  2018.  let me get this out of the way as  quickly as i can goku versus jiren round  two featuring the iconic perfect form of  ultra instinct took place this year now  i still feel that the first fight  slightly edges out the second one in  terms of the actual fighting and hype  behind him seven deadly sins also had  its blaze of glory here with the  exciting meliodus vs commandments fight  a fitting end before the animation went  to hell and it became meme fodder but i  still wish the next season's got way  more love it feels bad on how they  wasted meliodas versus eskenor with that  travesty of an adaptation  [Applause]  my hero academia also reached what i  feel is a good end point for a chunk of  the story with one for all and all might  clashing after years of build-up the  hype is completely justified here and it  serves as a fitting closure to the world  of my hero academia that we started with  the landscape and the name of the game  completely changed from that point  onward and that episode is worth the  watch even for that fight alone  none of those though won the fight of  the year in 2018. the winner that's the  momoshiki fight boruto may have its  whole slew of criticisms but for a  moment the sasuke and naruto vs  momoshiki fight made me forget about a  lot of those hey i can't help it now can  i see the two legends of the previous  series come together and kick ass once  again brought the kid out in me and i  couldn't help but immerse myself in the  battle even after stepping back and  looking at it from a more objective  perspective the fight does still hold up  it's a joy to watch with how their  powers and chemistry with each other  have developed through time  2019  if i were to talk about 2019 i'd be  talking about a lot of things favorite  fights were plenty and i could spend an  entire day talking about them maybe i  could go for one of mob's season 2  beautifully animated fights well that  time levi gave us a masterclass on how  to pivot a monumental sacrifice into  pure methodical destruction we've also  got the climax of the luffy versus  katakuri fight this year which easily  was one of my favorite fights in one  piece the heavens feel movies are also  screaming around about this time and  they really did the saber versus  berserker fight justice speaking of fate  babylonia still hasn't ended its run at  this point but we already got a very  good fight in gorgon vs ushiwakamaru as  well as the quetzalcoatl fight but  that's not what we're here for now is it  right we all know you're here for the  single most influential fight in anime  history in my opinion which of course is  tanjiro vs rui it pretty much sets the  bar for tv anime fights with how much it  enhanced what was already a goosebump  inducing moment in the manga ufo table  made magic happen and if you're still on  the fence about me calling this one of  the most influential fights in anime  history then let me ask you this  question where else did an anime fight  break the internet so much that it  turned an anime with decent popularity  into the sensation of the year overnight  it's still arguable but in my experience  never had i seen that phenomenon before  demon slayer not an event  not a plot twist but a fight a fight  that was able to catapult its series  into never before seen heights i mean  that's just unheard of if we're going  with influence in the community combined  with the animation and a bit of context  there's little doubt that demon slayer  takes the crown  2020  so demon slayer fever was in full swing  in 2020 and it capitalizes on the  momentum by releasing the infinity train  movie that caps off with one of the most  emotional battles in the series rengoku  vs akaza  [Applause]  now normally i would have been tempted  to pen this as a winner candidate  outright if not for the serious clause i  had then again even if it's not for such  clause this fight narrowly loses out to  another theatrical ufo table production  2020 also saw the grand finale of the  heavens feel movie and with it comes the  winner of 2020s fight of the year shiro  and ryder vs saber alter at this point  we're being desensitized to spectacular  fight choreography and effect you can  blame ufo table for that fights of this  quality have become so normalized now  but this one deserves a special mention  for how it finally put shiro and ryder's  strategy against sabre's sheer unmatched  power as seen in the previous movies we  also get to see ryder go all out which  is a treat because the poor servant has  been a glorified jobber in other routes  on the side of tv anime we have the  attention catching glipe near fight that  allowed the show to start off with some  momentum for such a niche title fgo also  ended with a theomath fight and a  barrage of noble phantasms that  shattered my expectations for a mobile  game adaptation if there's one thing  that god of high school is really really  good for it's just a showcase of fights  heck the running joke is that this  series is just fight after fight after  fight and while i lean towards agreeing  with that at least the guys behind the  production committee did the fight  pretty competently chinese anime fights  like the often featured fog kill fights  in the hitori noshita ones also debuted  here more on those on my old video that  you can access up there  overall 2020 has been a great year for  fights despite the delays and other  real-life circumstances that should have  hampered production  2021  we've finally reached the present  congratulations there's quite a lot to  be said for 2021 so let's get some of  the honorable mentions out of the way  after showcasing its worth through a lot  of epic battles and hype moments black  clover goes out with a banger of a final  arc the fight that led to that arc  arsenal and the army versus dante and  it's every bit as cool as fans made it  out to be naruto and sasuke also team up  again and this time in a far less  successful battle against g-game however  this got the shonen community busting  again and i find it funny yet sad that  one of the only times boruto seems to  gain this amount of traction are when  the legacy characters are involved in a  big way i also gave vv the nod for  action anime of the year and i can say  that the whole diva versus hugo segment  does deserve a mention gintama ended  this year with gintama the final movie  it gave us kintoki vs utsuro another  amazing fight with a lot of emotional  weight man i'm gonna miss that series so  much  once i look at the year however i think  that i can safely give the crown to  hanami versus yuji and todo  move over ufo table mafa is ready to  step up to the plate and while it felt  difficult to choose amongst the numerous  masterfully crafted fights in jiu jitsu  kaizen i gave this fight the win  why it feels like the one with the most  hype behind it sure gojo broke the  internet to a lesser extent yeah nanami  and megumi both got to show off their  cool stuff even novara got to show off  her sadistic and dangerous sight however  if you look at context and what the  fights mean for the protagonist seeing  the master student tandem of yuji and  toto team up against the big boss is  such a joy  and that's a wrap it's been a decade of  epic anime fights and the cool thing  about this is that i barely touch the  tip of the iceberg i'm sure that lost in  the shuffle are countless hidden gems  and i'd ask you to introduce me to some  of them so how did you find this video  if you liked it hit the like button and  tell me in the comment section so that i  know whether you're fond of the new  direction i'm taking with these lists if  you're up for some monetary support be  sure to check out my patreon and  memberships thank you for watching this  list it's been a fun ride through memory  lane with you all i hope to see you next  time and i wish you a good day
 

